title: script:stop
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Scripting the GUI]]
kind: reference
summary: Ask the running script to stop (the one asking, by default)

Asks a script the GUI started to stop: `SIGTERM` to its whole process group, which a script may trap to finish what it is doing. Without an argument, the script asking the question on screen — what Escape does while a question is up; with a run id (`script-3`), that one. With no question on screen and no run id it is refused: a question of a workspace out of sight is not the one meant, and nothing else is stopped or closed. Once the script is gone the GUI closes the workspaces it opened and gives their slots back. A script that ignores the signal goes on: <<cmd "script:kill">> ends it. A question nobody owns is closed instead ([[Script sessions]]).
